.claude/

# Tile packages (downloaded, not source)
tile-packager/*.lock
tile-server/*.lock

# Runtime content (pushed bundles + uploaded assets)
# `data/*`, NOT `data/` — git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a
# nested `!data/roads/` under a bare `data/` never re-includes anything. That
# was invisible for data/buildings only because those files were already
# tracked when the exception was written, and gitignore does not apply to
# tracked files. Excluding the ENTRIES instead lets the negations below work.
data/*
# ...EXCEPT the OSM vector extracts. See docs note below.
#
# data/ is packager OUTPUT and rightly ignored — 189 MB of raster tiles from
# CARTO / EOX / Esri, none of which we are licensed to redistribute, so caching
# them in the repo would be a WORSE licence position than streaming them.
#
# data/buildings is different on both counts. It is ~1.3 MB of OSM footprints
# under ODbL — free to redistribute with attribution, which /wiki already
# carries — and it is the ONLY source for the offline buildings tier
# (world/buildings-geojson). Ignoring it made that tier structurally
# undeliverable: install.sh points TILE_DIR at ${INSTALL_DIR}/data, inside the
# git checkout, and git pull IS the deploy mechanism — so an ignored path is one
# the fleet can never receive. Tracking it means the tier ships with the code.
#
# data/roads is tracked for the same two reasons, as of the CARTO removal.
# It is 4.1 MB of ODbL road centrelines, and it is now the ONLY source for the
# night street grid (world/roads-geojson) — the CartoDB raster it replaced was
# 132 MB of the tile cache and Enterprise-only for commercial use. The size
# argument runs the same way: 4.1 MB rides `git pull` to the fleet today, where
# the 2.7 GB tile rsync never has.
!data/buildings/
!data/roads/

# ⚠ `data/*` above is ROOT-ANCHORED — a pattern with an internal slash is —
# while the bare `data/` it replaced matched at ANY depth. This path silently
# stopped being covered and 18k packager tiles turned up untracked. Re-stated.
tools/tile-packager/data/

# graphify knowledge-graph output (regenerable)
graphify-out/
src/graphify-out/

# Local agent tooling state (not project source)
.context/
.serena/
.codex/
outputs/
